From 5e536b6a49724c2b70bdd7ca51b00e49428c2223 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:21:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] nx2: passthrough backend step 1, a host RM channel following
 one guest channel

EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH=1 (Linux, NVIDIA open kernel driver; build with
EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_SDK=<driver src dir>): an RM client, VA space, TSG and
AMPERE_CHANNEL_GPFIFO_A channel with ADA_A, ADA_COMPUTE_A and
AMPERE_DMA_COPY_B, set up as the USCL passthrough tools do. Each GPFIFO entry
of the first guest channel becomes one serialized host submission (a semaphore
release the CPU waits for). The guest's own methods are not submitted yet:
that needs the guest VA space mirrored (step 2). Any failure logs and leaves
the backend off; the RM client is freed at shutdown and at exit.

MKW racing: 15.45M entries, mean 3-8 us per submission, worst ~3 ms, no Xid;
racing fps 37-43 -> 13-21 with the per-entry wait, so later steps must not
wait per entry.
---
 src/video_core/CMakeLists.txt      |  11 +
 src/video_core/dma_pusher.cpp      |   7 +
 src/video_core/gpu.cpp             |   2 +
 src/video_core/nx2_passthrough.cpp | 402 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/video_core/nx2_passthrough.h   |  24 ++
 5 files changed, 446 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/video_core/nx2_passthrough.cpp
 create mode 100644 src/video_core/nx2_passthrough.h

