+// NVIDIA GPU passthrough backend (EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH=1, Linux, NVIDIA open kernel driver, built with
+// EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_SDK): the guest's channels run on the host GPU through the driver's RM ioctls.
+// Step 1 (channels and submission): one host channel follows the first guest channel; each of its GPFIFO
+// entries becomes one serialized host submission (a semaphore release the CPU waits for). The guest's own
+// methods are not submitted yet (they need the guest VA space mirrored, step 2); Vulkan still renders.
+namespace Tegra::Nx2Passthrough {
+
+/// Called for every guest command list as the DMA pusher parses it (once per entry).
+void OnEntry(s32 channel, GPUVAddr address, std::span<const CommandHeader> commands);
